<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="031" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>The single re-evaluating scheduled job, with episodes, secure-child ownership and per-item today</title>
    <phase>3 Evaluator, Signal lifecycle and read</phase>
    <gate>030, 003, 007, 008, 009, 024, 037, 039, 098 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Background workload placement decision plus the mechanism that prevents the worklist rotting; writes the first real Signals.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Follows ADR-036 with six live reference implementations; the owner decisions (D-13, D-25, D-32, D-33) fix every judgement call.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Tasks 025, 032, 033, 034, 038 and 101 all attach to this job or its evaluation core.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>030, 003, 007, 008, 009, 024, 037, 039, 098</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,scheduled-job,signals</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-1.5 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build ONE re-evaluating scheduled job that upserts Signals whose predicate now holds and closes those whose predicate no longer holds, in one pass, around a side-effect-free Evaluate(version, scope) core; implement the episode-scoped key before the first Signal is written, write Signals on Secure matters as secure children (no Restricted/Limited skip, D-33), and judge Date Only comparisons per item in the assignee's time zone.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer. One component deciding both directions.</role>
  <goal>A nightly ADR-036 IScheduledJob that re-evaluates every enabled policy (both lanes), creates, re-raises and closes Signals with episode-scoped keys, writes Secure-matter Signals through the resolver ownership path (task 039), and stamps sprk_lastevaluated on everything it touches; its evaluation core is reusable read-only by the admin dry run.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Path B's window is relative to now, so the predicate truth value changes even when nobody writes anything. Of four state transitions, TWO have no event to hook: death by time (the communication ages out) and birth by time (an old budget revision ages out, re-truthing the notExists half). So the nightly pass cannot be closure-only, and event-driven evaluation alone would never fire ConditionCleared. Owner decisions 2026-10-07 (spec section 9) add four binding changes: D-13 episode-scoped key and re-raise rule (the built writer keeps a Resolved row Resolved and the key is unique, so without episodes a resolved Signal can never come back, #13); D-15's skip of Restricted and Limited matters is WITHDRAWN by D-33 (those settings exclude only external contacts; the staff wall is the Secure flag, and Signals on Secure matters become secure children through task 039, notes/secure-signals-scoping.md); D-32 re-raises still-true subjects when a policy is switched Off then On; D-25 "today" per item in the assignee's, else owner's, else UTC time zone, the same rule as To Do generation (task 098); D-23 witness values are evidence lines. Reconciliation B.2 row 031 (M-7, #39): the evaluation core must be side-effect free and reusable by the admin dry run (task 101).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReevaluationJob.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalEvaluator.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalWriter.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/ExternalAccess/SecureRecordIsolationCensusJob.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalCallerContext.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/RegistrationModule.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">Scope: implement IScheduledJob. NO new hand-rolled timer BackgroundService.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-052">Scope: this workload runs in the BFF. Tie-breaker is fewer moving parts; the workload is hundreds of rows, not a scale problem. State the placement decision in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: ONE component that both creates and closes. Do NOT build an evaluator plus a separate sweep: two components can disagree about the same Signal, which miscounts suppression in both directions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (reconciliation B.2, #39): split the work into a side-effect-free core, Evaluate(version, scope) returning per subject the hit, the grouping matter, the witness evidence and the facts, and the writing job that wraps it. Evaluate writes nothing, takes no lock, and can run against one matter (event triggers, task 032) or all (nightly, admin dry run, task 101).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-13): BEFORE THE FIRST SIGNAL IS WRITTEN, change SignalWriter.BuildDedupeKey to {policycode}|{type}|{id}|{episode}. For a hit, find the subject's latest Signal for the policy by a begins-with query on sprk_dedupekey: none, start episode 1; latest Open or Acknowledged, reconcile it (same episode); latest Resolved, re-raise as episode n+1 only when the subject is not suppressed (sprk_suppresseduntil in the future blocks it) AND, Decide lane, the latest episode did not end in a dismissal less than quietWindowDays ago (the compiled predicate's knob, default 14 days), or, Do lane, the subject's current due date differs from the resolved Signal's sprk_duedate. A latest episode closed as Superseded re-raises under the new version whenever the new version holds. Task 007 already re-keyed existing rows as episode 1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-33, replaces D-15's skip): do NOT skip Restricted or Limited matters; they get Signals normally. Ownership on Secure matters is the writer's resolver path from task 039; a resolver REFUSAL is a skip that is logged and counted in the run metric (dimension skipped_refused). The ONE other skip is D-33's narrow case: a To Do subject with no matter that is filed under a Secure project (its Decision Record would have no lineage); skip it, log at Information with a stable EventId and count it (dimension skipped_secure_no_matter). No other skip.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-32): when a policy that was switched Off is switched On again, the pass re-raises, as new episodes, the subjects whose latest episode closed as PolicyRetired and whose predicate still holds (the same not-suppressed condition applies). A Retired (statuscode Retired) policy is not re-enabled by this rule.</constraint>
<constraint source="owner">COORDINATION WITH uac-r2 (owner 2026-10-07): (1) Before starting, fetch origin/master and re-read the current uac-r2 implementation this task depends on, and name the files (with commit) in the completion record: SecureChildLineage.cs, config/secure-record-owner-role.json, RecordOwnershipResolver (I-6), RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter, CallerRecordAccessProbe, tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs, ADR-034 and its amendments, ExternalCallerContext (ADR-003), CoreAncestorResolver (FR-26 core-ancestor stamps, D-34). (2) Check uac-r2's open PRs and active work for overlap (gh pr list --state open; the uac-r2 current-task.md and TASK-INDEX in C:\code_files\spaarke-wt-unified-access-control-r2 if present) and run /conflict-check. (3) Reuse uac-r2's mechanisms; never build a parallel one. Any change to uac-r2-owned files (the lineage list, the owner-role config, the ledger) goes through uac-r2's review, with the PR linked in this task. (4) If the uac-r2 code has changed in a way that invalidates this plan, STOP and escalate rather than adapting silently.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-25): for a compiled predicate whose filter compares a Date Only column (task 024 marks them), judge "today" per item: the item's assignee's time zone, else its owner's, else UTC, using the SAME shared helper as task 098's To Do generation (DataverseUserTimeZone). Do not write a second time-zone helper. Path B (a date-time column compared with now-Nd) keeps the single WindowAnchorUtc.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-23, FR-48): write sprk_evidencerefs as evidence lines: one witness per exists clause (the matching communication, its sender and received date, the clause id from task 026 if present), plus context lines marked context, not tested. Witness values never enter sprk_sentence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (FR-16 amended, #15): the pass never closes a Signal that is already Resolved (a decision-closed Signal stays Acted).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: cadence derives from the EXISTING sprk_lane column. Decide-lane policies run here AND on the event triggers; Do-lane policies run here ONLY. Do not add a per-policy trigger column.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: stamp sprk_lastevaluated on every Signal the pass touches, so a stale Signal is distinguishable from an unevaluated one.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: sprk_rankscore and severity are NOT computed here: the rank formula and the severity source are open (spec section 11 Q1, section 11.1 O-1, O-2). Ordering is task 038's.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: if this task changes src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api, state the Placement Justification in the PR citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md, and measure publish size against a FRESH build of master from a short path with file counts compared on both sides. Ceiling 60 MB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: any test this task adds that asserts a Dataverse column list, entity name or option-set value must be paired with something touching the real schema. A consistently throwing path is a defect to diagnose, never noise to tolerate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: before opening a BFF PR, run /conflict-check. 56 of 62 active projects declare a hot path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">OWNER DECISION 2026-10-04: no silent failure. The writer fails closed by design, so a broken credential, a refused privilege or a dead job would otherwise look exactly like 'no conditions found'. The evaluator therefore (a) emits an App Insights custom metric per run (ontology.evaluator.runs, dimension outcome = succeeded|failed, plus signals written/updated/closed/re-raised/skipped_refused/skipped_secure_no_matter counts), following the existing custom-metric pattern the alerts in infrastructure/bicep/modules/alerts.bicep consume; (b) logs every writer refusal (credential, token, privilege, escalation) at Error with a stable EventId and increments ontology.writer.failures (dimension reason); (c) records the time of the last SUCCESSFUL run and exposes it on a DIAGNOSTIC health check tagged so it lands on /healthz/catalog-style diagnostics, NOT on the /healthz liveness probe (a stale evaluator must not recycle instances).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">FROM TASK 030 REVIEW R13 (2026-10-04): the Signal writer does NOT set sprk_regardingrecordnumber (ADR-024 resolver set) or sprk_privilegeflagged (schema draft: 'copied forward', ADR-015), and no spec line assigns either to task 030. Decide here, with a spec citation, whether the evaluator supplies them (e.g. privilegeflagged copied from the subject when the Signal is built) and pass them to the writer; if neither belongs to this task, record which task owns them. A privilege flag that silently stays empty is the kind of gap ADR-015 exists to prevent. Details: notes/030-signal-writer-progress.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">OWNER-DERIVED GATE (2026-10-04, task 022 review F6): obtain every compiled predicate ONLY through PolicyVersionValidator.TryPrepareForEvaluation(snapshot, subjectId, out compiled). Never call PredicateCompiler.Compile directly and never skip the gate: it is what logs EventId 50301 + meters an invalid policy and continues with the others (owner rule: validate at evaluation, fail closed, no silent failure). Build FactValues for the sentence ONLY from values read for the firing subject from POSITIVE fields (the subject's when filter and exists clauses), never from notExists clause fields (task 022 F5, section 0.3).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">FROM TASK 022 REVIEW ROUNDS 2-3 (2026-10-05): template tokens are limited to CompiledPredicate.TemplateEligibleFields. For a subject `when` field, put the firing subject's own value in FactValues. For an `exists`-clause field, the token is eligible only when that clause pins the field to one value, and FactValues carries that pinned literal. A `when` field filtered with `ne` (the `&lt;&gt;` operator) can match a subject whose value is NULL, which makes SignalWriter.RenderSentence refuse the write. Treat a null value for any token as a write refusal that is logged and metered (no silent skip), and test that case.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-34): "grouping matter" reads CORE record (matter or project) everywhere in this task. Evaluate returns each hit's core record as the writer derives it (task 037, CoreAncestorResolver); the "not suppressed" check in the re-raise rule reads suppression per (policy, core record) (FR-17 as amended), and per (policy, subject) for a D-35 item with no core record only if the owner confirms O-25 (until then, a D-35 item is never treated as suppressed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-35): a hit with no matter and no project is written through the writer's owner-only path (task 037) and is not skipped.</constraint>
  </constraints>

