  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code. Confirm 007, 008, 009, 024, 037 and 098 have landed.</step>
    <step order="1">Read SecureRecordIsolationCensusJob and one other IScheduledJob to establish the registration, lease and logging conventions.</step>
    <step order="2">Change BuildDedupeKey to the episode-scoped format and implement the latest-episode lookup and the D-13 re-raise rule (with unit tests) BEFORE any code path can write a Signal.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement Evaluate(version, scope): obtain the compiled predicate through TryPrepareForEvaluation, run it, apply D-33's narrow skip only, apply per-item today for Date Only comparisons (D-25), and build witness evidence (D-23); no writes.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the job: for each enabled policy, Evaluate then write via the writer (create, reconcile or re-raise); in the SAME pass close still-open Signals whose predicate no longer holds (task 033 supplies the closure semantics) and never re-close a Resolved one.</step>
    <step order="5">Stamp sprk_lastevaluated on every Signal touched; process both lanes.</step>
    <step order="6">Register the job and confirm it appears in the admin jobs endpoint.</step>
    <step order="7">Tests: creates; closes when the predicate stops holding; leaves open and refreshes; episode 2 re-raise after a dismissal once the quiet window passes and not before; Do-lane re-raise only after a date change; Off then On re-raise (D-32); Restricted/Limited written normally, resolver refusal skipped, D-33 narrow skip; per-item today across two time zones; Evaluate writes nothing.</step>
    <step order="8">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="9">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a full nightly re-evaluation proves too expensive at realistic data volumes, STOP and escalate to agree a scoping strategy rather than silently narrowing the pass to recently-changed rows. Narrowing it reintroduces the birth-by-time blind spot that this design exists to close.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the uac-r2 code the writer's ownership path depends on (RecordOwnershipResolver, SecureChildLineage, the owner-role config) has changed since task 039 in a way that invalidates this plan, STOP and escalate rather than adapting silently.</trigger>
    <trigger>If task 098's shared time-zone helper is not on master when this task starts, STOP; do not write a second helper (D-25).</trigger>
    <trigger>D-34 gives a To Do filed under a Secure project a core record (the project) and its Decision Record a lineage lookup (sprk_project), which removes the premise of D-33's narrow skip. Whether the skip is retired is not decided (O-24): keep applying it and ask the owner.</trigger>
    <trigger>CoreAncestorResolver also treats sprk_workassignment and sprk_servicerequest as CORE; D-34 names only matter or project. If an item's core record is a work assignment or service request (spec section 11.1 O-22), STOP and ask the owner; do not fall back to a matter or to Not filed on your own.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Six IScheduledJob implementations exist, but none evaluates policies or manages Signal lifecycle. The Signal writer (task 030) writes one Signal; it does not decide episodes, skips or closure.</existing>
    <extension>No. The existing jobs are domain-specific reconciliations; this is a new workload. The ADR-036 seam itself IS being reused rather than a new scheduling mechanism built, and the writer is extended (BuildDedupeKey) rather than replaced.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Nothing closes a Signal when its condition clears on its own, so the worklist fills with stale items, users mute it, and suppression miscounts because an auto-cleared Signal is indistinguishable from a human dismissal. Without episodes a resolved Signal never returns; without the skip, secured matters leak; without per-item today, the Do lane disagrees with the Briefing by a day.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET</tool>
  </tools>

