  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an enabled policy whose predicate now holds for a matter, when the job runs, then a Signal exists for it with a key ending in |1.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an open Signal whose predicate no longer holds, when the job runs, then it is closed with a resolution type and no Decision Record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an open Signal whose predicate still holds, when the job runs, then it stays open and sprk_lastevaluated is refreshed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Decide Signal dismissed 10 days ago whose predicate still holds and a quiet window of 14 days, when the job runs, then no new Signal is raised; at 15 days, then episode 2 is raised.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a resolved Do-lane Signal whose subject's due date is unchanged, when the job runs, then nothing is raised; after the due date changes and the predicate holds, then episode n+1 is raised.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a suppressed subject (sprk_suppresseduntil in the future), when the job runs, then nothing is raised.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a hit on a Restricted or a Limited matter, when the job runs, then a Signal is written normally (D-33).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a hit on a Secure matter, when the job runs, then the Signal is written through task 039's path and owned by the Secure Record Owners team; given a resolver refusal, then nothing is written and skipped_refused is counted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an overdue To Do with no matter filed under a Secure project, when the job runs, then no Signal is written and skipped_secure_no_matter is counted; given an overdue To Do with no matter and no Secure root, then a Signal is written (D-31).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a policy switched Off (its open Signals closed as PolicyRetired) and then On again, when the job runs, then each subject whose predicate still holds and is not suppressed is raised as a new episode (D-32).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given two overdue-task subjects whose assignees are in UTC-8 and UTC+10 with the same due date, when the job runs at a time when that date is yesterday in one zone and today in the other, then only the first is overdue.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given Evaluate(version, scope), when called, then it returns hits with witness evidence and performs no Dataverse write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Path B hit, when written, then sprk_evidencerefs carries one witness line per exists clause and sprk_sentence contains no witness value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a Resolved Signal is never closed again by the pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Do-lane policy, when the job runs, then it is evaluated (both lanes run nightly).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a disabled policy is not evaluated at all.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the job is an IScheduledJob and no new timer BackgroundService was added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The job is registered and visible via the admin jobs endpoint.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the writer refuses (e.g. empty writer client id), when the job runs, then the run is recorded with outcome=failed, an Error log carries the stable EventId, and ontology.writer.failures increments; it is never recorded as a successful run with zero Signals.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given no successful run for longer than the threshold, when the diagnostic health check is read, then it reports Unhealthy with the last-success time, and /healthz (liveness) is unaffected.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests cover the stated contract and edge cases above; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in task notes. All tests pass; the BFF builds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a hit on a subject filed under a project with no matter, when the job runs, then the Signal groups under the project and suppression is read for (policy, that project) (D-34).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a hit on a To Do with no matter and no project, when the job runs, then a Signal is written owned by the To Do's owner with both core-record columns null (D-35).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-03 (amended), FR-11, FR-12, FR-14 and FR-14a (amended, D-31, D-33), FR-15, FR-16 (amended, D-32), FR-17a, FR-47, FR-48; D-13, D-23, D-25, D-31, D-32, D-33 (D-15's skip withdrawn). design.md section 8.3 carries the reasoning, including the four-transition table. The ADR-040 amendment (task 003) is merged. Amended 2026-10-07 for D-13..D-29: deps now include 007 (schema), 008 (role grants), 009 (re-seed), 024 (grammar), 037 (Do-lane writer subjects), 039 (secure-child ownership, added 2026-10-07 for D-33) and 098 (time-zone helper); Threshold (025) follows this task.</notes>

